            {
              "text": "When selecting a consultancy in Perth for business workflow automation and **Microsoft Power Automate** (and the broader Microsoft Power Platform), the right choice largely depends on your organization’s size, industry, and the complexity of your systems (e.g., standard M365 flows vs. enterprise ERP/CRM robotic process automation).\n\nThe leading consultancies in Perth are grouped by their strengths and target market:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Enterprise & High-Scale Systems Partners\n*Best for large enterprises, government departments, and mining/resources requiring complex system architectures, multi-environment governance, and deep Dynamics 365 / Azure integration.*\n\n* **Velrada (an ASG / Nomura Company)**\n  * **Location:** St Georges Terrace, Perth CBD\n  * **Profile:** Velrada is widely regarded as one of Australia’s premier Microsoft partners and is headquartered in Perth. They specialize in large-scale Power Platform implementations, complex Power Automate Desktop (RPA) workflows, and integrating automations across Dynamics 365, Dataverse, and Azure.\n  * **Best for:** Enterprise-grade automation frameworks, resources/mining sector workflows, and full digital transformation programs.\n\n* **Data#3 (Perth Office)**\n  * **Location:** Belmont / Perth\n  * **Profile:** As one of Australia’s largest Microsoft Solutions Partners, Data#3 has an established local presence in WA. They possess deep experience in cloud licensing, infrastructure, and setting up enterprise Power Platform **Center of Excellence (CoE)** toolkits and Data Loss Prevention (DLP) automation governance.\n  * **Best for:** Large commercial and public sector clients that require governance, security compliance, and licensing optimization alongside workflow design.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Mid-Market, Specialized & Industry-Focused Consultancies\n*Best for mid-sized organizations, non-profits, healthcare, and education looking for high-touch local support and pragmatic business solutions.*\n\n* **illuminance Solutions**\n  * **Location:** Perth CBD\n  * **Profile:** An award-winning Microsoft Solutions Partner that has gained national and global recognition (including Microsoft Partner for Social Impact). While they do enterprise work, they have an exceptional reputation for using Power Automate and Power Apps to modernize operational workflows in human services, government, and community sectors.\n  * **Best for:** NDIS, Aged Care, community services, education, and mid-tier enterprises wanting seamless CRM and approval automations.\n\n* **Bremmar Consulting**\n  * **Location:** Perth\n  * **Profile:** Bremmar focuses heavily on the Not-for-Profit, Aged Care, and mid-market commercial spaces in WA. They specialize in practical Microsoft 365 workflow automations (e.g., policy approval chains, HR onboarding, intranet file routing) that run on an organization's existing licensing.\n  * **Best for:** Organizations needing to cut down administrative debt without massive custom engineering costs.\n\n* **Scope Logic**\n  * **Location:** West Perth\n  * **Profile:** A proactive IT consultancy and Microsoft Partner that focuses on modern workplace integration. They specialize in combining Power Automate with Power BI and Power Apps to create closed-loop, data-driven operational processes.\n  * **Best for:** Mid-sized commercial businesses needing integrated reporting, automated notifications, and streamlined departmental handoffs.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Boutique Automation & Flow Specialists\n*Best for fast turnaround, workflow audits, unravelling “shadow IT” flows, and targeted Microsoft 365 plumbing.*\n\n* **BIZ-LYNX Technology**\n  * **Location:** Perth\n  * **Profile:** Known for personalized, hands-on consulting across Microsoft 365, SharePoint architecture, and Power Automate. They focus on helping local businesses replace manual forms, email-based approvals, and repetitive data entry with reliable cloud flows.\n  * **Best for:** Growing businesses wanting a local team for design, training, and troubleshooting.\n\n* **Scalify / Doohickey**\n  * **Location:** Perth-based\n  * **Profile:** These boutique practices focus heavily on **automation debt audits** and lean implementations. They help companies audit orphaned flows, fix failing approval loops, and integrate AI Builder (for document and invoice data extraction) without unnecessary subscription bloat.\n  * **Best for:** Fixed-scope builds, auditing broken or legacy flows, and AI-assisted document processing.\n\n---\n\n### Key Questions to Ask When Choosing:\n\n1. **Cloud Flows vs. Desktop RPA:** If your workflows interact with modern APIs (Microsoft 365, Salesforce, Xero), standard Cloud Flows are sufficient. If you need bots to interact with legacy on-premise software via UI clicking, confirm the consultancy has hands-on **Power Automate Desktop (RPA)** certification.\n2. **Licensing & Connector Costs:** Many basic flows are included in Microsoft 365 Business licenses, but premium connectors (e.g., SQL, HTTP webhooks, Dataverse) trigger per-user or per-flow licensing. A reputable consultant should model this cost up front.\n3. **Governance and CoE:** Without governance, employees build flows on personal accounts that break when someone leaves the company. Ensure your partner uses **Service Principals**, sets up proper environment management, and documents error-handling protocols.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
